[
	[
		"\n"
	],
	[
		"\n"
	],
	[
		"\n"
	],
	null,
	null,
	[
		"a\nb"
	]
]
-- End --

The capture groups which the `m` flag introduces stay invisible to the script:
the groups of the pattern as written keep their numbering, however many lists
the rewriting wraps and however deeply the groups are nested.

-- Testcase --
{%
	printf("%.J\n", [
		match("a1b", /(\D)(\d)(\D)/m),
		match("a\nb", /([^x])(\d?)([^y])/m),
		length(match("a\nb", /([^x])(\d?)([^y])/m)),
		match("a", /(([^x]))/m),
		match("a\n(a)", regexp("[^x]\\u0028a\\u0029", "m")),
		"" + regexp("[^x]a", "ms")
	]);
%}
-- End --

